# This repository IS the Spec-Agentic-SDLC corpus, not a repository that adopted it.
#
# `scripts/bash/adopt.sh` deliberately does not copy this file, so a repository that adopted the
# corpus does not carry it. `check-corpus.sh` reads its presence to decide whether to run the
# checks that audit the corpus governing ITSELF — mutation coverage, the measurement series, the
# red-team ratchet, the upstream pin, the changelog of this project. Those checks are meaningless
# in an adopting repository and, before this marker existed, produced seventeen failures and two
# Python tracebacks on a fresh adoption (#106).
#
# Declared rather than inferred. Guessing from the presence of `docs/adr/` or of the spec-kit pin
# would have been wrong in both directions: the governed layer copies both.
corpus: valdomirosouza/Spec-Agentic-SDLC
